# Experiment integrity

- Treat `../synthetic-lung-ct-evaluation` as read-only.
- Never alter evaluator thresholds, calibration, mock benchmark logic, or scoring during a parameter search.
- Never commit weights, medical images, environments, or generated runs.
- During mock optimization, edit only `workspace/candidate.json`.
- Keep cases and seeds fixed when comparing candidates.
- Use the fixed `data/dsr-valid/manifest.json` selection for real DSR comparisons.
- Do not add, remove, or replace DSR cases during a parameter search.
- Save every run and report regressions as well as improvements.
- Do not train or fine-tune without explicit human authorization.
